@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Learning

@*
    KnowledgeCategoryCard — the Design's .catcard (motiva-student.css:74-81).

    WHY THIS IS NOT AN MCard
    ------------------------
    MCard's surfaces are all "border present at rest": Default draws a hairline
    border, AmbientEdge draws a permanent 1px gradient rule. The Design's
    category card is the opposite — a masked ::before that is a flat hairline at
    rest and *thickens* through 1px -> 1.5px -> 2px as it goes hover -> active,
    with the gradient only appearing on interaction. Expressing that through
    MCard would mean adding a fourth variant whose only consumer is this screen,
    which is exactly the "Knowledge-Center-specific duplicate of a primitive"
    the brief warns against. So the interaction lives here and the tokens stay
    shared.

    Rendered as a real <button> (the prototype uses a click-only <div>) so
    keyboard activation, focus order and aria-expanded come for free.
*@

<div class="kc-cat" style="--kc-accent:@Category.Accent">
    <button type="button"
            class="kc-cat-card @(IsOpen ? "kc-cat-card-open" : "")"
            aria-expanded="@(IsOpen ? "true" : "false")"
            aria-controls="@PanelId"
            @onclick="OnToggle">

        <span class="kc-cat-icon">
            <KnowledgeIcon Category="Category.Key" Size="18" />
        </span>

        <span class="kc-cat-text">
            <span class="kc-cat-label">@Category.Label</span>

            @*
                DELIBERATE ADDITION — the Design renders the label alone, though
                its own view-model computes `cat.count` (Motiva Resources.dc.html:574)
                and never uses it.

                It can afford that because every sample category is populated. The
                real taxonomy is fixed and two of its four categories are empty
                today, so a label-only grid gives a student no way to tell a full
                category from an empty one without clicking each in turn. The count
                is a Design-computed value surfaced, not a new idea.
            *@
            <span class="kc-cat-count">@CountLabel</span>
        </span>
    </button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public KnowledgeCategory Category { get; set; } = default!;

    [Parameter] public int Count { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool IsOpen { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnToggle { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Id of the panel this card expands, for aria-controls. The page
    /// owns the panel, so it owns the id.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? PanelId { get; set; }

    private string CountLabel => Count switch
    {
        0 => "אין פריטים",
        1 => "פריט אחד",
        _ => $"{Count} פריטים",
    };
}
